## Scope

This overlay covers the **technological** Annex-A controls that arbiter can
mechanically enforce. Organizational, people, and physical controls (A.5/A.6/A.7)
remain manual and are tracked separately in the Annex-A coverage matrix. The
controls below are the enforceable subset; each row names the gate that produces
the evidence of conformity.

## Controls → gate map

| Annex-A | Control | Bound arbiter gate (fail-closed) | Evidence produced |
| ------- | ------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------- |
| A.8.25 | Secure development life cycle | `node scripts/check-all.mjs` (L1/L2/L3 tiers) + module-boundary rules (dependency-cruiser / ArchUnit) | Gate pass record per merge; architecture conformance report |
| A.8.26 | Application security requirements | OWASP / ZAP dynamic application security testing (DAST) + STRIDE threat model | DAST scan report; documented threat model |
| A.8.28 | Secure coding | Static application security testing (SAST: eslint-security / semgrep) + dependency vulnerability scan (`npm audit` / trivy fs) | SAST findings = 0 high; dependency scan report |
| A.8.29 | Security testing in development and acceptance | Secret scanning (`gitleaks`) + PII scan (`pii-scan`) + the security test suite | gitleaks clean; pii-scan clean; security tests green |
| A.8.32 | Change management | Commit-footer rationale audit (**INV-119**, change-management evidence) + ff-only PR/gate process (INV-101) | Per-commit rationale trailer; gated PR history |

## Access control (A.5.15 / A.8.4)

Source-code access and change authorization are enforced, not documented:

- **Branch protection** + **CODEOWNERS** require review on every protected path.
- **INV-23** forbids direct pushes to `main` — all change flows through a gated PR.
- Result: no source-code change reaches the protected branch without an
  authenticated, reviewed, gated path (A.8.4 *Access to source code*).

## SBOM / supply-chain integrity (A.5.21)

Supply-chain assurance for the ICT supply chain (A.5.21 *Managing information
security in the ICT supply chain*) is produced by the release pipeline:

- **SBOM** generation + **cosign** signing + **SLSA** provenance attestation on
  release artifacts.
- **Dependency vulnerability scan** (`npm audit` / trivy fs) gates
  on known-vulnerable transitive dependencies.

## How to use this matrix

Each row is an auditable claim: run the named gate, attach its output as the
evidence of conformity for that control. Because the gates are the same ones the
project already runs in CI, ISO 27001 conformity for this subset is a byproduct
of a green pipeline — re-run `node scripts/check-all.mjs` to regenerate the
evidence. Controls outside this enforceable subset are tracked manually in the
Annex-A coverage matrix.

